const DATA_MT = {"tema":[{"id":"MT-4","nama":"Dari Kuadratik ke Kewangan","tingkatan":4,"warna":"#e8a33d"},{"id":"MT-5","nama":"Dari Ubahan ke Pemodelan","tingkatan":5,"warna":"#d9534f"}],"topik":[{"id":"MT-T4-1","tema":"MT-4","nama":"Fungsi dan Persamaan Kuadratik","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 4, Bab 1: Fungsi dan Persamaan Kuadratik","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 4, Bab 1: Fungsi dan Persamaan Kuadratik","negeri":"perlis","pin":0,"xy":[73.8,74.0],"nota":["Ungkapan kuadratik berbentuk ax² + bx + c dengan a ≠ 0; graf ialah parabola.","a > 0: titik minimum, graf terbuka ke atas; a < 0: titik maksimum, graf terbuka ke bawah.","Paksi simetri: x = −b/2a.","Punca persamaan kuadratik: pemfaktoran, penyempurnaan kuasa dua atau rumus x = (−b ± √(b² − 4ac)) / 2a.","Diskriminan b² − 4ac: > 0 dua punca berbeza, = 0 dua punca sama, < 0 tiada punca nyata.","Hasil tambah punca = −b/a; hasil darab punca = c/a."],"kod":"1"},{"id":"MT-T4-2","tema":"MT-4","nama":"Asas Nombor","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 4, Bab 2: Asas Nombor","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 4, Bab 2: Asas Nombor","negeri":"perak","pin":0,"xy":[125.5,111.2],"nota":["Asas 2 menggunakan digit 0 dan 1; asas 5 menggunakan 0–4; asas 8 menggunakan 0–7.","Nilai tempat asas n: n⁰, n¹, n², ... dari kanan.","Asas n ke asas 10: darab setiap digit dengan nilai tempat dan tambah.","Asas 10 ke asas n: bahagi berulang dengan n, baca baki dari bawah ke atas.","Antara asas selain 10: tukar ke asas 10 dahulu.","Penambahan dan penolakan asas n dilakukan seperti asas 10 tetapi 'membawa' apabila mencapai n."],"kod":"2"},{"id":"MT-T4-3","tema":"MT-4","nama":"Penaakulan Logik","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 4, Bab 3: Penaakulan Logik","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 4, Bab 3: Penaakulan Logik","negeri":"perak","pin":0,"xy":[117.5,133.2],"nota":["Pernyataan ialah ayat yang boleh ditentukan benar atau palsu, bukan kedua-duanya.","Negasi menukar nilai kebenaran; 'dan' benar jika kedua-duanya benar; 'atau' benar jika sekurang-kurangnya satu benar.","Implikasi 'Jika p maka q'; akas 'Jika q maka p'; songsangan 'Jika bukan p maka bukan q'; kontrapositif 'Jika bukan q maka bukan p'.","Kontrapositif sentiasa mempunyai nilai kebenaran sama dengan implikasi asal.","Argumen deduktif: premis umum → kesimpulan khusus; aruhan: contoh khusus → kesimpulan umum.","Contoh penyangkal membuktikan sesuatu pernyataan umum palsu."],"kod":"3"},{"id":"MT-T4-4","tema":"MT-4","nama":"Operasi Set","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 4, Bab 4: Operasi Set","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 4, Bab 4: Operasi Set","negeri":"kelantan","pin":0,"xy":[159.8,111.2],"nota":["Persilangan A ∩ B: unsur sepunya; kesatuan A ∪ B: semua unsur dalam A atau B.","Pelengkap A′: unsur dalam set semesta yang bukan dalam A.","n(A ∪ B) = n(A) + n(B) − n(A ∩ B).","n(A′) = n(ξ) − n(A).","Hukum De Morgan: (A ∪ B)′ = A′ ∩ B′ dan (A ∩ B)′ = A′ ∪ B′.","Gambar rajah Venn memudahkan penyelesaian masalah bilangan unsur."],"kod":"4"},{"id":"MT-T4-5","tema":"MT-4","nama":"Rangkaian dalam Teori Graf","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 4, Bab 5: Rangkaian dalam Teori Graf","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 4, Bab 5: Rangkaian dalam Teori Graf","negeri":"terengganu","pin":0,"xy":[183.0,119.5],"nota":["Graf terdiri daripada bucu (titik) dan tepi (garis).","Darjah bucu = bilangan tepi yang bertemu di bucu itu.","Jumlah darjah = 2 × bilangan tepi.","Pokok: graf bersambung tanpa kitaran; n bucu mempunyai n − 1 tepi.","Graf berwajaran menyimpan nilai (jarak, kos, masa) pada tepi.","Jalan terpendek dan pokok rentang minimum menyelesaikan masalah rangkaian."],"kod":"5"},{"id":"MT-T4-6","tema":"MT-4","nama":"Ketaksamaan Linear dalam Dua Pemboleh Ubah","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 4, Bab 6: Ketaksamaan Linear dalam Dua Pemboleh Ubah","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 4, Bab 6: Ketaksamaan Linear dalam Dua Pemboleh Ubah","negeri":"terengganu","pin":0,"xy":[207.0,165.5],"nota":["Garis sempadan dilukis penuh untuk ≤ dan ≥; putus-putus untuk < dan >.","Uji titik (0, 0) untuk menentukan rantau yang memuaskan ketaksamaan.","Pintasan-x: set y = 0; pintasan-y: set x = 0.","Sistem ketaksamaan: rantau memuaskan ialah rantau bertindih.","'Sekurang-kurangnya' bermaksud ≥; 'tidak melebihi' bermaksud ≤.","Ketaksamaan linear digunakan untuk membuat keputusan dalam situasi had sumber."],"kod":"6"},{"id":"MT-T4-7","tema":"MT-4","nama":"Graf Gerakan","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 4, Bab 7: Graf Gerakan","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 4, Bab 7: Graf Gerakan","negeri":"pahang","pin":0,"xy":[157.8,201.5],"nota":["Laju = jarak ÷ masa; jarak = laju × masa; masa = jarak ÷ laju.","Graf jarak-masa: kecerunan = laju; garis mengufuk = pegun.","Graf laju-masa: kecerunan = pecutan; luas di bawah graf = jarak.","Pecutan = (v − u) ÷ t; pecutan negatif = nyahpecutan.","Purata laju = jumlah jarak ÷ jumlah masa.","1 km/j = 1/3.6 m/s."],"kod":"7"},{"id":"MT-T4-8","tema":"MT-4","nama":"Sukatan Serakan Data Tak Terkumpul","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 4, Bab 8: Sukatan Serakan Data Tak Terkumpul","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 4, Bab 8: Sukatan Serakan Data Tak Terkumpul","negeri":"selangor","pin":0,"xy":[122,212],"nota":["Julat = maksimum − minimum.","Julat antara kuartil = Q3 − Q1.","Varians = Σ(x − min)² ÷ N = Σx²/N − min².","Sisihan piawai = √varians.","Sisihan piawai kecil: data tertumpu dekat min, lebih konsisten.","Tambah nilai tetap tidak mengubah serakan; darab dengan k mengubah serakan sebanyak k kali."],"kod":"8"},{"id":"MT-T4-9","tema":"MT-4","nama":"Kebarangkalian Peristiwa Bergabung","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 4, Bab 9: Kebarangkalian Peristiwa Bergabung","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 4, Bab 9: Kebarangkalian Peristiwa Bergabung","negeri":"nsembilan","pin":0,"xy":[160.2,235.8],"nota":["Peristiwa bebas: P(A dan B) = P(A) × P(B).","Peristiwa bersandar (tanpa pulangan): kebarangkalian kedua dikira selepas peristiwa pertama berlaku.","Saling eksklusif: P(A atau B) = P(A) + P(B).","Tidak saling eksklusif: P(A atau B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A dan B).","P(sekurang-kurangnya satu) = 1 − P(tiada).","Ruang sampel membantu menyenaraikan semua hasil yang mungkin."],"kod":"9"},{"id":"MT-T4-10","tema":"MT-4","nama":"Matematik Pengguna: Pengurusan Kewangan","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 4, Bab 10: Matematik Pengguna: Pengurusan Kewangan","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 4, Bab 10: Matematik Pengguna: Pengurusan Kewangan","negeri":"johor","pin":0,"xy":[235.5,282.0],"nota":["Lima langkah pengurusan kewangan: tetapkan matlamat, nilai kedudukan, wujudkan pelan, laksanakan, kaji semula.","Matlamat SMART: Specific, Measurable, Attainable, Realistic, Time-bound.","Pendapatan aktif (gaji, komisen) dan pasif (sewa, dividen).","Perbelanjaan tetap dan tidak tetap; keutamakan keperluan daripada kehendak.","Aliran tunai positif: pendapatan > perbelanjaan; negatif: sebaliknya.","Simpan dana kecemasan sekurang-kurangnya enam bulan keperluan asas."],"kod":"10"},{"id":"MT-T5-1","tema":"MT-5","nama":"Ubahan","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 5, Bab 1: Ubahan","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 5, Bab 1: Ubahan","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[483.8,177.0],"nota":["Ubahan langsung: y = kx, y/x tetap, graf garis lurus melalui asalan.","Ubahan songsang: y = k/x, xy tetap, graf hiperbola.","Ubahan boleh melibatkan kuasa: y ∝ x², y ∝ √x, y ∝ 1/x².","Cari k daripada satu set nilai, kemudian guna untuk nilai lain.","Ubahan bergabung: contoh y = kx/z.","Jika jejari digandakan, luas bulatan menjadi empat kali ganda."],"kod":"11"},{"id":"MT-T5-2","tema":"MT-5","nama":"Matriks","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 5, Bab 2: Matriks","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 5, Bab 2: Matriks","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[345.8,233.0],"nota":["Peringkat matriks = bilangan baris × bilangan lajur.","Matriks sama jika peringkat sama dan unsur sepadan sama.","Tambah atau tolak: peringkat mesti sama, operasi pada unsur sepadan.","Darab skalar: setiap unsur didarab dengan skalar.","Darab matriks: lajur matriks pertama = baris matriks kedua; AB ≠ BA secara umum.","Matriks identiti I: AI = IA = A."],"kod":"12"},{"id":"MT-T5-3","tema":"MT-5","nama":"Matematik Pengguna: Insurans","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 5, Bab 3: Matematik Pengguna: Insurans","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 5, Bab 3: Matematik Pengguna: Insurans","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[463.8,233.0],"nota":["Risiko: kemungkinan kerugian yang tidak dapat ditentukan; insurans memindahkan risiko kepada syarikat.","Insurans hayat melindungi kematian, penyakit kritikal, hilang upaya; insurans am melindungi harta dan lain-lain.","Premium hayat = (nilai muka ÷ 1000) × kadar.","Premium asas motor komprehensif = kadar RM1000 pertama + RM26 setiap RM1000 baki (Semenanjung); premium kasar = premium asas − NCD.","Deduktibel: bayaran = kos − deduktibel.","Ko-insurans: pampasan = (dibeli ÷ harus dibeli) × kerugian − deduktibel jika dibeli kurang daripada yang diperlukan."],"kod":"13"},{"id":"MT-T5-4","tema":"MT-5","nama":"Matematik Pengguna: Percukaian","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 5, Bab 4: Matematik Pengguna: Percukaian","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 5, Bab 4: Matematik Pengguna: Percukaian","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[337.8,283.0],"nota":["Cukai ialah sumber pendapatan kerajaan dan alat melaksanakan polisi.","Jenis cukai: pendapatan (LHDN), jalan (JPJ), pintu/taksiran (PBT), tanah (kerajaan negeri), CKHT.","Pendapatan bercukai = pendapatan − pengecualian − pelepasan.","Cukai = cukai banjaran + kadar × baki − rebat.","PCB dibandingkan dengan cukai: kurang bayar perlu dijelaskan, lebihan dipulangkan.","Kegagalan memfailkan atau mengelak cukai boleh dikenakan denda, penalti dan penjara."],"kod":"14"},{"id":"MT-T5-5","tema":"MT-5","nama":"Kekongruenan, Pembesaran dan Gabungan Transformasi","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 5, Bab 5: Kekongruenan, Pembesaran dan Gabungan Transformasi","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 5, Bab 5: Kekongruenan, Pembesaran dan Gabungan Transformasi","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[549.0,87.0],"nota":["Kongruen: bentuk dan saiz sama (SSS, SAS, ASA/AAS, RHS).","Isometri: translasi, pantulan, putaran — saiz dan bentuk tidak berubah.","Pembesaran: faktor skala k = panjang imej ÷ panjang objek; luas imej = k² × luas objek.","Pantulan paksi-x: (x, y) → (x, −y); paksi-y: (−x, y); garis y = x: (y, x).","Gabungan transformasi: hasil dua atau lebih transformasi berturut-turut.","Teselasi: corak berulang menutup permukaan tanpa ruang kosong atau pertindihan."],"kod":"15"},{"id":"MT-T5-6","tema":"MT-5","nama":"Nisbah dan Graf Fungsi Trigonometri","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 5, Bab 6: Nisbah dan Graf Fungsi Trigonometri","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 5, Bab 6: Nisbah dan Graf Fungsi Trigonometri","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[545.0,115.0],"nota":["sin = O/H, kos = A/H, tan = O/A.","Skema ASTC: Semua (I), Sin (II), Tan (III), Kos (IV) positif.","Nilai khas: sin 30° = 1/2, kos 60° = 1/2, tan 45° = 1.","Sudut rujukan digunakan untuk sudut 0°–360°.","Graf sin dan kos: kala 360°, amplitud 1; graf tan: kala 180°.","sin²θ + kos²θ = 1."],"kod":"16"},{"id":"MT-T5-7","tema":"MT-5","nama":"Sukatan Serakan Data Terkumpul","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 5, Bab 7: Sukatan Serakan Data Terkumpul","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 5, Bab 7: Sukatan Serakan Data Terkumpul","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[611.0,133.0],"nota":["Min data terkumpul = Σfx ÷ Σf (gunakan titik tengah kelas).","Kelas mod: kelas dengan kekerapan tertinggi.","Ogif: graf kekerapan longgokan melawan sempadan atas kelas.","Q1, median dan Q3 dibaca pada N/4, N/2 dan 3N/4.","Sisihan piawai = √(Σfx²/Σf − min²).","Sisihan piawai atau julat antara kuartil lebih kecil menunjukkan data lebih konsisten."],"kod":"17"},{"id":"MT-T5-8","tema":"MT-5","nama":"Pemodelan Matematik","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Sains Tingkatan 5, Bab 8: Pemodelan Matematik","buku":"Buku Teks Matematik KSSM Tingkatan 5, Bab 8: Pemodelan Matematik","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[573.0,155.0],"nota":["Model matematik: hubungan matematik yang menghuraikan situasi dunia sebenar.","Proses: kenal pasti masalah, andaian dan pemboleh ubah, gunakan matematik, tentusahkan, murnikan, lapor dapatan.","Soalan terbuka tidak mempunyai maklumat lengkap, sesuai untuk pemodelan.","Andaian memudahkan masalah dan dinyatakan dengan jelas.","Pemurnian model dilakukan jika keputusan tidak sesuai.","Contoh model: I = Prt, d = vt, C = 3 + 1.5d."],"kod":"18"}],"soalan":[]};
const DATA_BM = {"tema":[{"id":"BM-4","nama":"Dari Kata ke Ayat dan Karya","tingkatan":4,"warna":"#e8a33d"},{"id":"BM-5","nama":"Dari Ayat ke Wacana dan Sastera","tingkatan":5,"warna":"#5b9bd9"}],"topik":[{"id":"BM-T4-1","tema":"BM-4","nama":"Kata Tunggal, Kata Majmuk dan Kata Terbitan","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 4, Aspek Tatabahasa, Bentuk Kata, SP 5.1.1 dan 5.1.2","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"perlis","pin":0,"xy":[73.8,74.0],"nota":["Kata tunggal ialah kata yang belum menerima sebarang imbuhan, contohnya makan, rumah dan cantik.","Kata majmuk ialah gabungan dua kata atau lebih yang membentuk satu makna baharu, contohnya meja tulis, kereta api dan anak yatim.","Kata majmuk yang telah mantap ditulis serangkai, contohnya jawatankuasa, suruhanjaya, olahraga, setiausaha, kakitangan dan tanggungjawab.","Kata terbitan dibentuk melalui pengimbuhan: awalan, akhiran, apitan dan sisipan.","Contoh awalan: ber-, me-, pe-, ter-, di- dan se-. Contoh akhiran: -an, -kan dan -i. Contoh apitan: ber-an, me-kan, pe-an, ke-an dan per-an.","Awalan meN- berubah bentuk mengikut huruf pertama kata dasar. Huruf k, p, t dan s luluh, contohnya kutip menjadi mengutip, tulis menjadi menulis dan sapu menjadi menyapu."],"kod":"1"},{"id":"BM-T4-2","tema":"BM-4","nama":"Kata Ganda dan Akronim","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 4, Aspek Tatabahasa, Bentuk Kata, SP 5.1.3","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"perak","pin":0,"xy":[125.5,111.2],"nota":["Kata ganda ialah kata yang digandakan untuk membawa makna tertentu, contohnya buku-buku, jalan-jalan dan berlari-lari.","Kata ganda penuh menggandakan seluruh kata dasar, contohnya rumah-rumah dan kecil-kecil.","Kata ganda separa menggandakan sebahagian kata dasar dengan perubahan bunyi, contohnya lelaki, pepohon dan tetamu.","Kata ganda berentak ialah penggandaan dengan perubahan bunyi, contohnya sayur-mayur, kuih-muih dan hiruk-pikuk.","Akronim ialah singkatan yang dieja sebagai satu perkataan, contohnya Bernama, Tabung Haji, IPTA dan Petronas.","Singkatan berbeza daripada akronim: singkatan dieja huruf demi huruf (DBP, KPM), manakala akronim disebut sebagai satu kata (MARA, Bank Negara)."],"kod":"2"},{"id":"BM-T4-3","tema":"BM-4","nama":"Kata Nama dan Kata Kerja","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 4, Aspek Tatabahasa, Golongan Kata, SP 5.2.1 dan 5.2.2","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"perak","pin":0,"xy":[117.5,133.2],"nota":["Kata nama ialah perkataan yang menamakan orang, binatang, benda, tempat atau konsep.","Kata nama am ialah nama umum, contohnya guru, kucing dan sekolah. Kata nama khas ialah nama tertentu, contohnya Aminah, Pulau Langkawi dan Bahasa Melayu.","Kata nama abstrak ialah nama bagi sesuatu yang tidak dapat dilihat atau disentuh, contohnya kejayaan, keadilan dan kebahagiaan.","Kata kerja ialah perkataan yang menyatakan perbuatan atau keadaan.","Kata kerja transitif memerlukan objek, contohnya membaca buku. Kata kerja tak transitif tidak memerlukan objek, contohnya tidur dan berlari.","Kata kerja transitif aktif dan pasif: Ahmad membaca buku (aktif); Buku itu dibaca oleh Ahmad (pasif)."],"kod":"3"},{"id":"BM-T4-4","tema":"BM-4","nama":"Kata Adjektif dan Kata Tugas","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 4, Aspek Tatabahasa, Golongan Kata, SP 5.2.3 dan 5.2.4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"kelantan","pin":0,"xy":[159.8,111.2],"nota":["Kata adjektif ialah kata yang menerangkan sifat, keadaan atau ciri sesuatu kata nama, contohnya cantik, tinggi dan bersih.","Kata adjektif boleh menerima kata penguat seperti sangat, amat dan terlalu, contohnya sangat cantik.","Kata adjektif boleh menunjukkan perbandingan: lebih besar, paling besar dan sebesar.","Kata tugas ialah kata yang fungsinya melengkapkan ayat, seperti kata hubung, kata sendi nama, kata penegas dan kata seru.","Kata hubung menghubungkan perkataan, frasa atau ayat, contohnya dan, tetapi, kerana dan jika.","Kata sendi nama mendahului frasa nama, contohnya di, ke, dari, pada, untuk dan kepada."],"kod":"4"},{"id":"BM-T4-5","tema":"BM-4","nama":"Frasa","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 4, Aspek Tatabahasa, Frasa, SP 5.3.1","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"terengganu","pin":0,"xy":[183.0,119.5],"nota":["Frasa ialah binaan yang terdiri daripada satu perkataan atau lebih, dan menjadi unit dalam binaan klausa atau ayat.","Frasa nama ialah frasa yang mempunyai kata nama sebagai inti, contohnya guru baharu dan buku cerita itu.","Frasa kerja ialah frasa yang mempunyai kata kerja sebagai inti, contohnya sedang membaca dan telah pulang.","Frasa adjektif ialah frasa yang mempunyai kata adjektif sebagai inti, contohnya sangat cantik dan amat bijak.","Frasa sendi nama ialah frasa yang bermula dengan kata sendi nama, contohnya di kantin, kepada guru dan untuk kawan.","Dalam ayat, frasa nama biasanya menjadi subjek atau objek, manakala frasa kerja, adjektif dan sendi nama menjadi predikat."],"kod":"5"},{"id":"BM-T4-6","tema":"BM-4","nama":"Ayat Dasar, Ayat Tunggal dan Ayat Majmuk","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 4, Aspek Tatabahasa, Ayat, SP 5.3.2 dan 5.3.3","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"terengganu","pin":0,"xy":[207.0,165.5],"nota":["Ayat dasar ialah ayat paling ringkas yang terdiri daripada subjek dan predikat. Ia mengikut empat pola: FN + FN, FN + FK, FN + FA dan FN + FS.","Contoh ayat dasar: Ali guru (FN + FN); Ali berlari (FN + FK); Bunga itu cantik (FN + FA); Mereka di kantin (FN + FS).","Ayat tunggal ialah ayat yang mengandungi satu klausa, iaitu satu subjek dan satu predikat.","Ayat tunggal susunan biasa ialah subjek diikuti predikat. Ayat songsang meletakkan predikat sebelum subjek untuk penegasan, contohnya Sedang membaca buku murid itu.","Ayat majmuk ialah ayat yang mengandungi dua klausa atau lebih. Ia dibentuk melalui gabungan, pancangan atau campuran.","Ayat majmuk gabungan menggunakan kata hubung gabungan seperti dan, atau, tetapi, lalu dan malah."],"kod":"6"},{"id":"BM-T4-7","tema":"BM-4","nama":"Jenis Ayat","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 4, Aspek Tatabahasa, Ayat, SP 5.3.4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"pahang","pin":0,"xy":[157.8,201.5],"nota":["Ayat penyata (ayat berita) menyatakan maklumat atau penerangan, dan diakhiri tanda noktah.","Ayat tanya digunakan untuk bertanya. Ia terdiri daripada ayat tanya dengan kata tanya (apa, siapa, mengapa, bagaimana, bila, di mana) dan ayat tanya tanpa kata tanya (menggunakan -kah atau intonasi).","Ayat perintah mengandungi suruhan, larangan, silaan dan permintaan, contohnya Bukalah buku anda; Jangan merokok di sini.","Ayat seruan menyatakan perasaan seperti kagum, marah, sedih atau terkejut, dan menggunakan kata seru seperti wah, aduhai, cis dan oh, serta tanda seru.","Kata tanya 'adakah' digunakan di awal ayat tanya tanpa kata tanya khusus, contohnya Adakah dia sudah makan?","Ayat tanya ditulis dengan tanda soal; ayat seruan dengan tanda seru; ayat penyata dan perintah (biasa) dengan tanda noktah."],"kod":"7"},{"id":"BM-T4-8","tema":"BM-4","nama":"Peribahasa","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 4, Aspek Seni Bahasa, SP 4.2.1","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"selangor","pin":0,"xy":[122,212],"nota":["Peribahasa ialah ungkapan yang mengandungi pengajaran, sindiran, nasihat atau teguran dalam bahasa yang indah. Jenisnya termasuk simpulan bahasa, perumpamaan, pepatah, bidalan, perbilangan dan kata-kata hikmat.","Simpulan bahasa ialah gabungan dua kata atau lebih yang membawa makna baharu, contohnya ringan tulang (rajin), besar kepala (sombong) dan tangan panjang (suka mencuri).","Perumpamaan menggunakan kata bandingan seperti, bagai, umpama atau laksana, contohnya bagai aur dengan tebing dan seperti kucing dengan anjing.","Pepatah ialah ungkapan yang menjadi pedoman dan nasihat, contohnya biar lambat asal selamat.","Bidalan mengandungi nasihat dan pengajaran, contohnya bersatu teguh, bercerai roboh.","Peribahasa hendaklah digunakan mengikut konteks yang sesuai dan dieja dengan betul supaya makna tidak berubah."],"kod":"8"},{"id":"BM-T4-9","tema":"BM-4","nama":"Prosa dan Puisi (Seni Bahasa)","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 4, Aspek Seni Bahasa, SP 4.1.1, 4.1.2, 4.3.1, 4.3.2 dan 4.4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"nsembilan","pin":0,"xy":[160.2,235.8],"nota":["Prosa ialah karya bebas yang ditulis dalam bentuk perenggan, contohnya cerpen, novel dan drama. Puisi terikat kepada rangkap, baris, rima dan irama.","Unsur cerpen dan novel: tema, persoalan, watak dan perwatakan, plot, latar, gaya bahasa, nilai dan pengajaran.","Plot ialah susunan peristiwa dalam cerita: permulaan, perkembangan, konflik, klimaks dan peleraian.","Pantun mempunyai empat baris serangkap. Dua baris pertama ialah pembayang dan dua baris terakhir ialah maksud, dengan rima a-b-a-b.","Syair mempunyai empat baris serangkap, dengan rima a-a-a-a, dan setiap baris membawa maksud atau cerita. Seloka ialah puisi berunsur jenaka, sindiran atau ejekan.","Drama ialah karya yang dipersembahkan melalui dialog dan lakonan. Skrip drama mengandungi babak, watak, dialog dan arahan pentas."],"kod":"9"},{"id":"BM-T4-10","tema":"BM-4","nama":"Membaca, Memahami dan Menulis dengan Terancang","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 4, Kemahiran Membaca SP 2.2 dan 2.3; Kemahiran Menulis SP 3.4 dan 3.6","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"johor","pin":0,"xy":[235.5,282.0],"nota":["Idea utama ialah isi pokok yang diterangkan dalam sesebuah perenggan. Ia biasanya terdapat dalam ayat topik.","Perenggan yang baik mempunyai ayat topik, ayat huraian, ayat contoh dan ayat penutup.","Fakta ialah maklumat yang boleh dibuktikan benar. Pendapat ialah pandangan atau penilaian seseorang yang tidak semestinya benar.","Penanda wacana menghubungkan ayat dan perenggan, contohnya pertama, kedua, selain itu, tambahan pula, oleh itu dan kesimpulannya.","Karangan terdiri daripada pendahuluan, isi (perenggan huraian) dan penutup.","Semasa menyunting, semak ejaan, tanda baca, tatabahasa, kesesuaian laras dan kesinambungan idea."],"kod":"10"},{"id":"BM-T5-1","tema":"BM-5","nama":"Ejaan, Tanda Baca dan Penyuntingan","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 5, Kemahiran Menulis (hlm. 55) dan Aspek Tatabahasa (hlm. 59), Tingkatan 5","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[483.8,177.0],"nota":["Huruf besar digunakan pada huruf pertama ayat, nama khas, nama bulan, hari, gelaran dan nama bahasa, contohnya Cikgu Aminah, Bahasa Melayu dan Ogos.","Tanda koma digunakan untuk memisahkan perkataan dalam senarai, selepas kata penanda wacana (oleh itu,) dan sebelum atau selepas klausa tambahan.","Tanda noktah dua ( : ) digunakan sebelum senarai, contoh atau huraian, manakala tanda soal ( ? ) digunakan di hujung ayat tanya.","Kata sendi nama di dan ke ditulis terpisah daripada kata nama tempat (di sekolah, ke pasar), tetapi di- sebagai awalan kata kerja pasif ditulis rapat (dibaca, dimakan).","Kata ganti nama diri -ku, -mu dan -nya ditulis rapat dengan kata yang mendahuluinya, contohnya bukuku dan rumahnya.","Penyuntingan meliputi menyemak ejaan, tanda baca, tatabahasa, ketepatan fakta dan susunan idea sebelum karya dihantar."],"kod":"11"},{"id":"BM-T5-2","tema":"BM-5","nama":"Kata Hubung dan Penanda Wacana","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 5, Aspek Tatabahasa, Golongan Kata dan Menulis, Tingkatan 5 (hlm. 55 dan 59)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[345.8,233.0],"nota":["Kata hubung gabungan menghubungkan unsur yang setara: dan, atau, tetapi, lalu, malah, serta dan lagi.","Kata hubung pancangan menghubungkan klausa utama dengan klausa bawahan: bahawa, kerana, supaya, jika, apabila, walaupun, sebab, agar dan sehingga.","Penanda wacana menghubungkan perenggan dan idea, contohnya pertama, kedua, seterusnya, selain itu, tambahan pula, oleh itu, namun begitu dan kesimpulannya.","Gunakan kata hubung yang menunjukkan hubungan sebab (kerana, sebab), akibat (oleh itu), syarat (jika), pertentangan (tetapi, walau bagaimanapun) dan tujuan (supaya).","Jangan menggunakan dua kata hubung yang sama maksud serentak, contohnya 'agar supaya' dan 'walaupun ... tetapi'.","Kata hubung pancangan 'bahawa' digunakan selepas kata kerja seperti menyatakan, mengatakan dan percaya."],"kod":"12"},{"id":"BM-T5-3","tema":"BM-5","nama":"Ayat Aktif dan Ayat Pasif","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 5, Aspek Tatabahasa, Ayat, Tingkatan 5 (hlm. 59)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[463.8,233.0],"nota":["Ayat aktif ialah ayat yang subjeknya melakukan perbuatan, contohnya Ali menendang bola.","Ayat pasif ialah ayat yang subjeknya menerima perbuatan, contohnya Bola ditendang oleh Ali.","Hanya kata kerja transitif boleh menjadi ayat pasif.","Ayat pasif diri ketiga menggunakan awalan di-, contohnya Surat itu ditulis oleh Salmah.","Ayat pasif diri pertama dan kedua menggunakan kata ganti nama pertama (saya, kami, kita) atau kedua (awak, kamu) diikuti kata kerja tanpa imbuhan, contohnya Buku itu saya baca dan Tugasan itu awak siapkan.","Ayat pasif tidak menggunakan awalan di- pada ayat diri pertama atau kedua, dan tidak menggunakan meN- pada kata kerja pasif."],"kod":"13"},{"id":"BM-T5-4","tema":"BM-5","nama":"Ayat Majmuk: Gabungan, Pancangan dan Campuran","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 5, Aspek Tatabahasa, Ayat Majmuk, Tingkatan 5 (hlm. 59)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[337.8,283.0],"nota":["Ayat majmuk gabungan terbentuk apabila dua ayat atau lebih yang setara digabungkan dengan kata hubung gabungan.","Ayat majmuk pancangan terdiri daripada klausa utama dan klausa bawahan yang dipancangkan dengan kata hubung pancangan.","Pancangan relatif menggunakan 'yang', contohnya Murid yang rajin itu mendapat hadiah.","Pancangan komplemen menggunakan 'bahawa', contohnya Guru berkata bahawa peperiksaan akan bermula.","Pancangan keterangan menggunakan kata hubung seperti kerana, jika, apabila, supaya dan walaupun.","Ayat majmuk campuran ialah gabungan ayat majmuk gabungan dan pancangan dalam satu ayat."],"kod":"14"},{"id":"BM-T5-5","tema":"BM-5","nama":"Kesalahan Ayat dan Laras Bahasa","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 5, Aspek Tatabahasa dan Kemahiran Menulis, Tingkatan 5 (hlm. 55 dan 59)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[549.0,87.0],"nota":["Pleonasme ialah penggunaan perkataan yang berlebihan dan bermakna sama, contohnya para guru-guru, agar supaya dan demi untuk.","Bahasa rojak mencampurkan bahasa Melayu dengan bahasa lain tanpa keperluan, contohnya 'Saya akan buat presentation esok' sepatutnya 'Saya akan membuat pembentangan esok'.","Ayat tergantung ialah ayat yang tidak lengkap kerana tiada klausa utama, contohnya 'Kerana dia sakit.'","Kesalahan 'di mana' dan 'yang mana' sebagai kata hubung adalah pengaruh bahasa asing; gunakan 'tempat' atau 'yang'. Contohnya Rumah tempat dia tinggal.","Laras bahasa ialah ragam bahasa yang berbeza mengikut situasi: formal dalam surat rasmi dan ucapan, tidak formal dalam perbualan dan mesej santai.","Bahasa baku digunakan dalam penulisan rasmi, dengan sebutan baku, ejaan betul dan susunan ayat gramatis."],"kod":"15"},{"id":"BM-T5-6","tema":"BM-5","nama":"Peribahasa dan Gaya Bahasa","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 5, Aspek Seni Bahasa, Tingkatan 5 (hlm. 58)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[545.0,115.0],"nota":["Gaya bahasa ialah cara pengarang menggunakan bahasa untuk menjadikan karya lebih indah, hidup dan berkesan.","Simile ialah perbandingan langsung menggunakan kata seperti, bagai, umpama atau laksana, contohnya wajahnya seperti bulan purnama.","Metafora ialah perbandingan secara tidak langsung tanpa kata bandingan, contohnya dia bunga di taman ini.","Personifikasi memberikan sifat manusia kepada benda atau haiwan, contohnya angin berbisik di telingaku.","Hiperbola ialah gaya bahasa melebih-lebihkan sesuatu, contohnya suaranya menggegarkan seluruh alam.","Peribahasa dan gaya bahasa hendaklah digunakan dengan tepat mengikut konteks dan tidak berlebihan."],"kod":"16"},{"id":"BM-T5-7","tema":"BM-5","nama":"Unsur Karya Sastera: Sajak, Cerpen, Novel dan Drama","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 5, Aspek Seni Bahasa, Tingkatan 5 (hlm. 58)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[611.0,133.0],"nota":["Tema ialah idea pokok pengarang. Persoalan ialah isu-isu kecil yang menyokong tema.","Watak dan perwatakan: protagonis ialah watak utama; antagonis menentang protagonis. Perwatakan boleh dikesan melalui dialog, tindakan dan huraian pengarang.","Plot ialah susunan peristiwa. Teknik plot termasuk imbas kembali (peristiwa lampau) dan imbas muka (isyarat peristiwa akan datang).","Latar meliputi tempat, masa dan masyarakat. Latar boleh mempengaruhi suasana dan watak.","Sajak mengandungi unsur bentuk (rangkap, baris), diksi (pilihan kata), gaya bahasa, irama dan mesej atau nilai.","Nilai murni dan pengajaran ditunjukkan melalui tindakan watak dan akibat yang berlaku dalam cerita."],"kod":"17"},{"id":"BM-T5-8","tema":"BM-5","nama":"Penulisan: Karangan, Rumusan dan Penulisan Rasmi","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Melayu Tingkatan 5, Kemahiran Menulis, Tingkatan 5 (hlm. 55)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Melayu KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[573.0,155.0],"nota":["Karangan yang baik mempunyai pendahuluan yang menarik, isi yang berhuraian dan berfakta, serta penutup yang merumuskan.","Rumusan ialah ringkasan teks dengan mengekalkan isi penting, menggunakan ayat sendiri, tidak menyalin contoh dan huraian panjang, dan ayat saling bersambung.","Surat rasmi mengandungi alamat penghantar, tarikh, rujukan, alamat penerima, salam pembuka, tajuk, isi dan salam penutup. Penutup lazim ialah Sekian, terima kasih dan Yang benar.","Ucapan formal bermula dengan penghormatan kepada tetamu, diikuti isi ucapan dan ditutup dengan ucapan terima kasih.","Laporan mengandungi tajuk, pengenalan, butir kejadian atau aktiviti, kesimpulan dan penyedia laporan.","Penulisan rasmi menggunakan bahasa baku, nada sopan, ayat tepat dan tidak berbunga-bunga."],"kod":"18"}],"soalan":[]};
const DATA_BI = {"tema":[{"id":"BI-4","nama":"Asas Kemahiran Bahasa Inggeris","tingkatan":4,"warna":"#e8a33d"},{"id":"BI-5","nama":"Pemantapan Bahasa Inggeris","tingkatan":5,"warna":"#5b9bd9"}],"topik":[{"id":"BI-T4-1","tema":"BI-4","nama":"Listening: Main Ideas, Details and Attitudes","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 4, Listening SP 1.1.1, 1.1.2, 1.1.3 dan 1.1.5, Tingkatan 4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"perlis","pin":0,"xy":[73.8,74.0],"nota":["The main idea is the central point of a talk or text. Ask: what is this mostly about?","Specific details answer questions such as who, what, when, where, how many and why.","Listen for signal words: first, next, however, in conclusion. They show the order and direction of ideas.","Attitude and opinion are shown through word choice and tone, for example love, dislike, worried, delighted and disappointed.","Before listening, read the questions to predict what information you need. While listening, write keywords, not full sentences.","Complex questions often ask about reasons, comparisons or what the speaker implies, not only what is said directly."],"kod":"1"},{"id":"BI-T4-2","tema":"BI-4","nama":"Guessing Meaning from Context","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 4, Listening SP 1.2.1; Reading SP 3.1.3 dan 3.1.4, Tingkatan 4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"perak","pin":0,"xy":[125.5,111.2],"nota":["Context clues are the words and sentences around an unfamiliar word that help you guess its meaning.","Definition clues explain the word directly, for example: A habitat, or the natural home of an animal, is protected.","Synonym clues give a word with a similar meaning, for example: She was jubilant, or extremely happy.","Contrast clues use words such as but, however and unlike to show the opposite meaning, for example: Unlike his generous sister, he is stingy.","Example clues give examples to show meaning, for example: Nutritious foods such as vegetables and fruits.","After guessing, check using a dictionary or a digital resource, and check that the meaning fits the sentence."],"kod":"2"},{"id":"BI-T4-3","tema":"BI-4","nama":"Speaking: Explaining, Justifying and Using Register","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 4, Speaking SP 2.1.1 hingga 2.1.5, 2.2.1, 2.3.1 dan 2.4.1, Tingkatan 4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"perak","pin":0,"xy":[117.5,133.2],"nota":["To explain causes and consequences, use because, since, as a result, therefore and consequently.","To explain advantages and disadvantages of plans, use phrases such as one benefit is..., the main drawback is... and on the other hand...","To justify your point of view, state your opinion, give a reason and add an example: I believe..., because..., for example...","Express feelings such as amusement, anger and regret with suitable language: I find it hilarious, I am furious, I regret not...","Use formal register in speeches and interviews and informal register with friends. Formal register uses complete sentences and polite words.","To check understanding, repeat what a speaker said: So you mean that..., If I understand correctly, you said..."],"kod":"3"},{"id":"BI-T4-4","tema":"BI-4","nama":"Reading: Main Points, Details and Writer's Attitude","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 4, Reading SP 3.1.1, 3.1.2 dan 3.1.5, Tingkatan 4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"kelantan","pin":0,"xy":[159.8,111.2],"nota":["The main point of a paragraph is usually stated in the topic sentence, often the first sentence.","Skimming means reading quickly to get the general idea. Scanning means searching for specific information such as dates, names and numbers.","Supporting details give examples, facts, reasons or explanations that develop the main point.","The writer's attitude is shown through word choice (adjectives and adverbs), for example admirable, shocking, unfortunately and sadly.","Fact can be proven; opinion shows belief or judgement, for example Malaysia has thirteen states (fact) and Nasi lemak is the best food (opinion).","A summary includes only the main points, in your own words, without minor details."],"kod":"4"},{"id":"BI-T4-5","tema":"BI-4","nama":"Reading: Text Types and Features","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 4, Reading SP 3.1.6 dan 3.2.1, Tingkatan 4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"terengganu","pin":0,"xy":[183.0,119.5],"nota":["Texts differ by genre. Each genre has features at word, sentence and text levels.","A news report has a headline, a lead paragraph (who, what, when, where, why), quotes and past tense reporting.","An email or letter has a greeting, body and closing, and the language depends on the audience (formal or informal).","A blog or opinion article uses a personal voice, rhetorical questions and persuasive language.","A notice or advertisement uses short, clear information, headings, bold words and imperatives (Join us! Call now!).","To investigate national issues, read different print and digital sources, compare viewpoints and check that the source is reliable."],"kod":"5"},{"id":"BI-T4-6","tema":"BI-4","nama":"Writing: Explaining Visuals, Causes and Consequences","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 4, Writing SP 4.1.1 dan 4.1.2, Tingkatan 4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"terengganu","pin":0,"xy":[207.0,165.5],"nota":["To explain a chart, graph or table, first state what it shows, then describe the highest and lowest values, and finally explain trends.","Useful words for trends: increase, rise, decline, drop, remain stable, fluctuate. For comparison: higher than, lower than, the same as.","A pie chart shows proportions of a whole. A bar chart compares categories. A line graph shows change over time.","To explain causes, use because, due to, as a result of. To explain consequences, use as a result, therefore, consequently, leading to.","Use present tense for general facts and past tense for completed events in a chart.","Write an introduction, 2 to 3 body paragraphs with data and a short conclusion for a description of visuals."],"kod":"6"},{"id":"BI-T4-7","tema":"BI-4","nama":"Writing: Organising Ideas and Opinion Texts","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 4, Writing SP 4.1.3, 4.1.4, 4.1.5 dan 4.2.3, Tingkatan 4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"pahang","pin":0,"xy":[157.8,201.5],"nota":["An essay has an introduction, body paragraphs and a conclusion.","A strong paragraph has a topic sentence, supporting sentences with reasons and examples, and a concluding sentence.","Use connectors to link ideas: firstly, in addition, moreover, however, in contrast, finally, in conclusion.","In an opinion essay, state your stand clearly in the introduction, support it with reasons and examples, and restate it in the conclusion.","Express common feelings in writing: I was amused by..., I felt furious when..., I regret that...","Plan before writing, draft, then edit by checking content, organisation, language and accuracy, using feedback to improve."],"kod":"7"},{"id":"BI-T4-8","tema":"BI-4","nama":"Writing Accuracy: Punctuation, Spelling and Register","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 4, Writing SP 4.2.1, 4.2.2 dan 4.2.4, Tingkatan 4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"selangor","pin":0,"xy":[122,212],"nota":["Use capital letters for the start of sentences, proper nouns, days, months and the pronoun I.","Use a comma in lists, after introductory phrases and before conjunctions joining two independent clauses. Use an apostrophe for possession and contractions.","Common confusions: their (belonging to them), there (place), they're (they are); its (belonging to it) and it's (it is); your and you're; affect (verb) and effect (noun).","Spell commonly misspelled words correctly: receive, separate, definitely, necessary, environment and government.","Formal register avoids contractions and slang: do not, cannot, I would like to. Informal register allows contractions and casual words.","Match register to the audience: formal for principals and employers, informal for close friends."],"kod":"8"},{"id":"BI-T4-9","tema":"BI-4","nama":"Grammar: Tenses, Subject-Verb Agreement and Articles","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 4, Writing SP 4.2 (ketepatan bahasa), Tingkatan 4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"nsembilan","pin":0,"xy":[160.2,235.8],"nota":["Simple present tense is used for habits and general truths: She walks to school.","Simple past is used for completed actions: We visited the museum yesterday. Present perfect links the past to the present: I have finished my work.","Present continuous describes actions happening now: He is reading.","Subject-verb agreement: singular subjects take singular verbs (The student studies); plural subjects take plural verbs (The students study).","Use 'a' before consonant sounds and 'an' before vowel sounds, for example a book and an hour.","Use 'the' for specific or known things, and no article for general plural or uncountable nouns: Water is essential."],"kod":"9"},{"id":"BI-T4-10","tema":"BI-4","nama":"Literature in Action: Plot, Character, Theme and Style","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 4, Literature in Action SP 5.1.1, 5.1.2, 5.2.1 dan 5.3.1, Tingkatan 4","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 4","negeri":"johor","pin":0,"xy":[235.5,282.0],"nota":["Plot is the sequence of events: exposition, rising action, climax, falling action and resolution.","Characters can be protagonist (main character) or antagonist (opposes the protagonist). We learn about characters from what they say, do and think.","Theme is the central message, such as courage, friendship or honesty. Setting is the time and place.","Stylistic features include imagery, similes, metaphors, personification and symbolism, which help show character, events and place.","To respond to a text, explain how it makes you feel and why: This poem made me feel hopeful because...","Imaginative responses include writing a script, creating props for a short play or writing an alternative ending."],"kod":"10"},{"id":"BI-T5-1","tema":"BI-5","nama":"Listening: Longer Texts and Complex Questions","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 5, Listening, Tingkatan 5 (kemahiran Listening mengikut DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[483.8,177.0],"nota":["Longer listening texts such as interviews, talks and news reports require you to follow the main idea across several minutes.","Complex questions may ask about reasons, comparisons, implied meaning and speaker attitude, not only direct facts.","Note-taking strategy: write keywords and numbers, use arrows for cause and effect, and use abbreviations for common words.","Listen for stress and intonation. A rising tone may show a question or surprise; a falling tone shows a statement or certainty.","Distractors in multiple-choice questions mention words from the recording but give the wrong meaning. Check that the whole option matches what was said.","After listening, review your answers by checking if each answer is supported by what you heard."],"kod":"11"},{"id":"BI-T5-2","tema":"BI-5","nama":"Speaking: Discussing, Summarising and Presenting","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 5, Speaking, Tingkatan 5 (kemahiran Speaking mengikut DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[345.8,233.0],"nota":["In a discussion, express your view clearly, listen to others and respond politely: I see your point, but..., I agree to some extent.","To justify a view, give reasons and evidence: statistics, examples or experiences.","To summarise a story or text, state the main idea and key events in a few sentences without unnecessary details.","In a presentation, use a clear introduction, 2 to 3 main points and a conclusion. Use signposting such as Firstly, Next and To sum up.","Good delivery includes clear voice, eye contact, suitable pace and natural gestures.","To handle questions, listen carefully, repeat or paraphrase if needed and answer politely."],"kod":"12"},{"id":"BI-T5-3","tema":"BI-5","nama":"Reading: Inference, Fact and Opinion, Bias","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 5, Reading, Tingkatan 5 (kemahiran Reading mengikut DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[463.8,233.0],"nota":["Inference means working out meaning that is not directly stated, using clues in the text and your own knowledge.","Fact can be checked and proven. Opinion expresses belief, feeling or judgement.","Bias is a one-sided view that ignores other perspectives. Look for emotive words, missing evidence and unfair comparisons.","Purpose and audience: a text may aim to inform, persuade, entertain or advise.","Tone is the writer's attitude, such as formal, humorous, critical, optimistic or concerned.","To evaluate a text, ask: who wrote it, why, what evidence is given and is anything left out?"],"kod":"13"},{"id":"BI-T5-4","tema":"BI-5","nama":"Reading: Informational Texts (News, Emails, Notices, Advertisements)","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 5, Reading, Tingkatan 5 (kemahiran Reading mengikut DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sarawak","pin":0,"xy":[337.8,283.0],"nota":["Informational texts present facts for a practical purpose: news, notices, emails, advertisements, brochures and reports.","A notice states what, when, where and who to contact. Look for dates, venues and conditions.","Advertisements use persuasive devices such as slogans, rhetorical questions, exaggeration and testimonials.","A report or news article is organised with a headline, introduction, details and conclusion. Quoted speakers add credibility.","Charts, tables and diagrams provide data. Read the title, labels and units before interpreting.","When answering reading questions, find the answer in the text, support it with evidence and avoid adding outside opinions."],"kod":"14"},{"id":"BI-T5-5","tema":"BI-5","nama":"Writing: Formal and Informal Emails and Letters","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 5, Writing, Tingkatan 5 (kemahiran Writing mengikut DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[549.0,87.0],"nota":["A formal letter or email includes a greeting (Dear Sir/Madam), a clear purpose, polite language, a closing (Yours faithfully/Yours sincerely) and a name.","Use Yours faithfully when you begin with Dear Sir/Madam. Use Yours sincerely when you begin with Dear Mr/Ms + name.","An informal email to a friend can use contractions, a friendly tone and casual expressions, for example Hi Aina, Hope you're well!","Organise a letter: opening (why you are writing), body (details in clear paragraphs), closing (what you expect and thanks).","Use polite formal phrases: I am writing to enquire about..., I would be grateful if..., I look forward to your reply.","Proofread for spelling, punctuation and tone before sending."],"kod":"15"},{"id":"BI-T5-6","tema":"BI-5","nama":"Writing: Articles, Reviews and Reports","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 5, Writing, Tingkatan 5 (kemahiran Writing mengikut DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[545.0,115.0],"nota":["An article has a catchy title, an engaging introduction, well-developed body paragraphs and a strong conclusion.","A review gives details of a book, film or product, evaluates strengths and weaknesses and gives a recommendation.","A report is formal and objective, with a title, introduction, findings, conclusion and recommendations.","Use evaluative language in reviews: engaging, predictable, well-written, disappointing, highly recommended.","Use formal objective language in reports: it was found that, the majority of, it is recommended that.","Organise ideas with topic sentences and connectors, and support points with facts, examples or evidence."],"kod":"16"},{"id":"BI-T5-7","tema":"BI-5","nama":"Grammar: Conditionals, Passive Voice, Reported Speech and Connectors","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 5, Writing dan Speaking, ketepatan bahasa, Tingkatan 5","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[611.0,133.0],"nota":["First conditional: If + present simple, will + verb, for real possibilities. If it rains, we will stay at home.","Second conditional: If + past simple, would + verb, for unreal or unlikely situations. If I won the lottery, I would travel the world.","Third conditional: If + past perfect, would have + past participle, for imaginary past situations. If she had studied, she would have passed.","Passive voice: subject + be + past participle. The window was broken by the boy. It is used when the action is more important than the doer.","Reported speech shifts tenses back: 'I am tired' becomes He said he was tired. Time words also change: tomorrow becomes the next day.","Connectors: although and however show contrast; because and since show cause; therefore and consequently show result."],"kod":"17"},{"id":"BI-T5-8","tema":"BI-5","nama":"Literature: Poems, Short Stories and Novel Components","dskp":"DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris Tingkatan 5, Literature in Action, Tingkatan 5 (komponen sastera mengikut DSKP KSSM Bahasa Inggeris)","buku":"Buku Teks Bahasa Inggeris KSSM Tingkatan 5","negeri":"sabah","pin":0,"xy":[573.0,155.0],"nota":["Poetry uses imagery, rhyme, rhythm, repetition and figurative language to express feelings and ideas in compressed form.","A short story has a limited number of characters, a single main plot and a clear message. A novel has more characters, sub-plots and longer development.","Analyse plot, character, setting, theme and point of view. Point of view may be first person (I) or third person (he, she).","Support answers with evidence: quote or refer to events, dialogue and language in the text.","Moral values in literature include courage, honesty, kindness, perseverance and respect.","Imaginative responses: write a diary entry from a character's view, a letter to a character, a new ending or a dramatic script."],"kod":"18"}],"soalan":[]};
